        <mxCell id="n46" value="Actors are stick figures and use cases are ellipses, as required by UML.&lt;br&gt;The system boundary separates what Zoldify does from who asks for it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Layout rule: every association line stays inside one of three empty&lt;br&gt;corridors — left of the first column, between the two columns, and right&lt;br&gt;of the second. No line crosses an ellipse. GHN sits on the left with the&lt;br&gt;seller because both drive the same use case." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="1210" width="560" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
